Dune: Awakening is out for the first time on XBOX Series X|S, with a new fully single-player mode. Learn why now is the best time to play.
Dune: Awakening Arrives on XBOX With New Ways to Play
Dune: Awakening has been out for a while on PC, but today it’s finally on XBOX. This isn’t just a port on a new platform. Over the past year we’ve been making the game more accessible and customizable for a wider group of players.
Dune: Awakening is an open-world survival game set on Arrakis, the desert planet central to the Dune universe. In the game you explore the deserts, gather resources, craft equipment, build a base and develop your character as you go through the story. Along the way, you’ll uncover the mystery of the missing Fremen.
If you wanted to explore Arrakis but thought Dune: Awakening wasn’t for you, read on. The XBOX launch introduces a single-player mode, full gameplay customization, the conclusion to Book One, and much more.&nbsp;
Dune: Awakening now includes a full single-player mode . When starting out, you can choose between three difficulty presets or customize every gameplay setting in detail.&nbsp;
When Dune: Awakening launched, there were too many ways to lose progression. Several quality-of-life improvements have been made to remove this kind of frustration from the game.&nbsp; &nbsp;
The Landsraad, Dune: Awakening ’s faction vs. faction endgame, has been completely rebuilt into a mission ‑ driven framework that works equally well for multiplayer PvE and single-player.&nbsp;Progress through twenty ranks from outsider to Atreides Envoy or Harkonnen Enforcer and unlock powerful rewards.&nbsp;
Dune: Awakening has arrived on XBOX Series X|S and the Microsoft Store with the complete experience and console-tailored UI and controls. Two graphics modes: Performance (60fps, Dynamic 4K) and Quality (30fps, Dynamic 4K). XBOX Series X renders at higher native resolution in both modes and adds enhanced visuals.&nbsp;
